                <pb facs="0372" n="290" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg290"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/661.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-08-19"><hi rendition="#italic">August 19,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The minister says he will recognize the Government of Gen. Leconte, in accordance
                    with the Department’s instructions, and suggests that in the course of the day
                    an American warship be instructed to fire a salute.</p>
            </div>
